artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $T(t)=\sum_{k=1}^n a_k e^{i\lambda_k t}$ denote a (complex-valued) trigonometric polynomial on $\mathbb{R}$, where $n\in\mathbb{N}$, $a_k\in\mathbb{C}$, and $\lambda_k\in\mathbb{R}$ are pairwise distinct frequencies. For $1\le r<\infty$ define
$$\|T\|_r=\Bigl(\sum_{k=1}^n |a_k|^r\Bigr)^{1/r},$$
and let $AP^r(\mathbb{R},\mathbb{C})$ denote the completion of the space of trigonometric polynomials with respect to $\|\cdot\|_r$.

Consider in addition the following classical spaces of almost periodic functions on $\mathbb{R}$:
- $AP^1$: almost periodic functions with absolutely convergent Fourier series (the case $r=1$ above);
- $AP$: the Bohr almost periodic functions, i.e. the uniform closure of trigonometric polynomials under $\|f\|_\infty=\sup_{t\in\mathbb{R}}|f(t)|$;
- $S$: the Stepanov space, the completion of trigonometric polynomials under the Stepanov norm $\|f\|_S=\sup_{x\in\mathbb{R}}\int_x^{x+1}|f(t)|\,dt$;
- $APW$: the Weyl space, the completion under the Weyl seminorm $\|f\|_W=\lim_{\ell\to\infty}\sup_{x\in\mathbb{R}}\frac{1}{\ell}\int_x^{x+\ell}|f(t)|\,dt$;
- $B^p$ ($1\le p<\infty$): the Besicovitch spaces, completion under $\|f\|_{B^p}=\bigl(\limsup_{\ell\to\infty}\frac{1}{2\ell}\int_{-\ell}^{\ell}|f(t)|^p\,dt\bigr)^{1/p}$;
- $PAP$: the space of pseudo almost periodic functions, i.e. functions of the form $f=g+\varphi$ with $g\in AP$ and $\varphi$ a bounded continuous function on $\mathbb{R}$ satisfying $\lim_{\ell\to\infty}\frac{1}{2\ell}\int_{-\ell}^{\ell}|\varphi(t)|\,dt=0$.

For each $r$ with $1<r<2$, determine the precise inclusion or non-inclusion relations between $AP^r(\mathbb{R},\mathbb{C})$ and each of the spaces $AP^1$, $AP$, $S$, $APW$, $B^p$ (for $1\le p<\infty$), and $PAP$.

